---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProsePage from '../components/ui/ProsePage.astro';

const updated = '13 October 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy | TommyTools"
	description="Privacy Policy for TommyTools: browser-local processing intent, analytics policy, Google Fonts disclosure, and what we collect today."
>
	<ProsePage title="Privacy Policy">
		<p><time datetime="2026-10-13">Last updated: {updated}</time></p>

		<p>
			This page describes how <strong>TommyTools</strong> (`tools.tommyfx.pk`) handles privacy
			<strong>based on the code and services in use today</strong>. Claims about local processing
			only apply when a specific tool states that behavior and the implementation matches it.
		</p>

		<h2>Browser-local processing (intent)</h2>
		<p>
			Core tools are designed to process inputs in your browser. When a tool says work stays on
			your device, that tool must not upload your files or sensitive inputs to our servers for
			processing. If a future tool needs a network request, that page will say so clearly.
		</p>
		<p>
			We do not offer user accounts, cloud file storage, or a product database in v1. There is no
			server-side file conversion pipeline for core tools today.
		</p>

		<h2>What we collect today</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Product analytics are off by default.</strong> The site includes an optional,
			privacy-limited analytics helper. It loads Google Analytics 4
			<strong>only when the operator sets</strong> <code>PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID</code> at build
			time. If that variable is empty (the normal case), no analytics script is loaded and no
			product events are sent.
		</p>
		<p>
			When analytics is enabled, the helper may send only these event names:
			<code>tool_start</code>, <code>tool_complete</code>, and <code>tool_export</code>, plus a
			coarse <code>tool_id</code> (the tool’s route slug, for example <code>work-hours</code>).
			We do <strong>not</strong> send file contents, uploaded bytes, timesheet values, calculator
			inputs, checklist answers, or other sensitive form data to analytics.
		</p>
		<p>
			Hosting and CDN providers (for example Cloudflare Pages, when the site is deployed) may
			process standard technical logs such as IP address, user agent, and requested URLs as part
			of delivering the site. That is infrastructure logging, not an application feature that
			reads your tool inputs.
		</p>

		<h2>Third-party resources</h2>
		<p>
			This site currently loads fonts from Google Fonts (`fonts.googleapis.com` /
			`fonts.gstatic.com`). Your browser may contact Google’s servers to fetch those font files.
			We do not send your tool inputs to Google Fonts.
		</p>

		<h2>Ads</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Ads are off by default.</strong> The layout can reserve separate ad zones
			<em>below</em> tools and in the help rail when the operator sets
			<code>PUBLIC_ADS_ENABLED=true</code>. Those zones do not sit on upload controls, primary
			action buttons, or result areas. No AdSense script is loaded until the operator confirms
			eligibility (SOP §12) and wires an approved unit. If ads are turned on, this policy will be
			updated with the provider details.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Questions about this policy: see <a href="/contact">Contact</a>.
		</p>
	</ProsePage>
</BaseLayout>
